.SS ":eyeglasses: Spec Compliance"
Add support for Flow shorthand import type (\fR#267\fP) (Jeff Morrison)

.PP
This change implements flows new shorthand import syntax and where previously you had to write this code:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import {someValue} from "blah";
import type {someType} from "blah";
import typeof {someOtherValue} from "blah";
.fi
.PP

.PP
you can now write it like this:

.PP
.PP
.nf
import {
  someValue,
  type someType,
  typeof someOtherValue,
} from "blah";
.fi
.PP

.PP
For more information look at \fRthis\fP pull request\&.

.PP
flow: allow leading pipes in all positions (\fR#256\fP) (Vladimir Kurchatkin)

.PP
This change now allows a leading pipe everywhere types can be used: 
.PP
.nf
var f = (x): | 1 | 2 => 1;

.fi
.PP

.PP
Throw error when exporting non-declaration (\fR#241\fP) (Kai Cataldo)

.PP
Previously babylon parsed the following exports, although they are not valid: 
.PP
.nf
export typeof foo;
export new Foo();
export function() {};
export for (;;);
export while(foo);

.fi
.PP
