.SS ":eyeglasses: Spec Compliance"
Throw error for reserved words \fRenum\fP and \fRawait\fP (\fR#195\fP) (Kai Cataldo)

.PP
\fR11\&.6\&.2\&.2 Future Reserved Words\fP

.PP
Babylon will throw for more reserved words such as \fRenum\fP or \fRawait\fP (in strict mode)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
class enum {} // throws
class await {} // throws in strict mode (module)
.fi
.PP

.PP
Optional names for function types and object type indexers (\fR#197\fP) (Gabe Levi)

.PP
So where you used to have to write

.PP
.PP
.nf
type A = (x: string, y: boolean) => number;
type B = (z: string) => number;
type C = { [key: string]: number };
.fi
.PP

.PP
you can now write (with flow 0\&.34\&.0)

.PP
.PP
.nf
type A = (string, boolean) => number;
type B = string => number;
type C = { [string]: number };
.fi
.PP

.PP
Parse flow nested array type annotations like \fRnumber[][]\fP (\fR#219\fP) (Bernhard Häussner)

.PP
Supports these form now of specifying array types:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var a: number[][][][];
var b: string[][];
.fi
.PP
