.SS ":eyeglasses: Spec Compliance"
Add static errors for object rest (#149) (\fR@danez\fP)

.PP
.RS 4
https://github.com/sebmarkbage/ecmascript-rest-spread 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Object rest copies the \fIrest\fP of properties from the right hand side \fRobj\fP starting from the left to right\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
let { x, y, \&.\&.\&.z } =  { x: 1, y: 2, z: 3 };
// x = 1
// y = 2
// z = { z: 3 }
.fi
.PP
.SS "New Syntax Errors:"
\fBSyntaxError\fP: The rest element has to be the last element when destructuring (1:10) 
.PP
.nf
> 1 | let { \&.\&.\&.x, y, z } = { x: 1, y: 2, z: 3};
    |           ^
# Previous behavior:
# x = { x: 1, y: 2, z: 3 }
# y = 2
# z = 3

.fi
.PP

.PP
Before, this was just a more verbose way of shallow copying \fRobj\fP since it doesn't actually do what you think\&.

.PP
\fBSyntaxError\fP: Cannot have multiple rest elements when destructuring (1:13)

.PP
.PP
.nf
> 1 | let { x, \&.\&.\&.y, \&.\&.\&.z } = { x: 1, y: 2, z: 3};
    |              ^
# Previous behavior:
# x = 1
# y = { y: 2, z: 3 }
# z = { y: 2, z: 3 }
.fi
.PP

.PP
Before y and z would just be the same value anyway so there is no reason to need to have both\&.

.PP
\fBSyntaxError\fP: A trailing comma is not permitted after the rest element (1:16)

.PP
.PP
.nf
let { x, y, \&.\&.\&.z, } = obj;
.fi
.PP

.PP
The rationale for this is that the use case for trailing comma is that you can add something at the end without affecting the line above\&. Since a RestProperty always has to be the last property it doesn't make sense\&.

.PP
